error[NK1214]: `p` moves forward, but it is a position of a text chosen at run time: a position moves only in one text.
  --> tests/text_pos_of_a_text_chosen_at_run_time_is_refused.nika:7:5
   |
 7 |     let q = p.forward(scalars: 1) ?? return ""
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A position is a byte offset below the language: a move is handed the text the position came from, which the compiler follows through names and branches (ADR-374 D4, D5).
   = help: Take the position from the text the move walks: `t.start()`, `t.end()` or a match of `t.find(…)`, bound by a `let` in this function; a scanner that keeps its place holds a `text::Cursor`.
error[NK1214]: `a` is cut at `p`, a position of a text chosen at run time.
  --> tests/text_pos_of_a_text_chosen_at_run_time_is_refused.nika:8:5
   |
 8 |     return a.after(p).clone()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A position is a boundary in exactly one text, the one it was taken from; in another it may fall inside a scalar, or read the wrong place (ADR-374 D5).
   = help: Take the position from `a` itself: `a.start()`, `a.end()`, or a match of `a.find(…)`.
2 type errors
